{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"type VoiceTrainingStatus = \"ready\" | \"training\" | \"failed\";","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2906","children":[{"type":"text","value":"packages/ai/src/types.ts:2906"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Whether a created voice is usable."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'ready'"},{"type":"text","value":" — usable in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateSpeech()"},{"type":"text","value":" now. Every adapter today returns\nthis, because they all finish the voice inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"generateVoice()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'training'"},{"type":"text","value":" — the provider accepted the request but is still building\nthe voice, so it is not usable yet. Reserved for providers that train\nasynchronously; no adapter returns it yet, and reading the state back\nwill land with the first adapter that needs it."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"'failed'"},{"type":"text","value":" — the provider finished without producing a usable voice."}]}]}]}],"headings":[]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\ntype VoiceTrainingStatus = \"ready\" | \"training\" | \"failed\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:2906](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2906)\n\nWhether a created voice is usable.\n\n- `'ready'` — usable in `generateSpeech()` now. Every adapter today returns\n  this, because they all finish the voice inside `generateVoice()`.\n- `'training'` — the provider accepted the request but is still building\n  the voice, so it is not usable yet. Reserved for providers that train\n  asynchronously; no adapter returns it yet, and reading the state back\n  will land with the first adapter that needs it.\n- `'failed'` — the provider finished without producing a usable voice.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: VoiceTrainingStatus\ntitle: VoiceTrainingStatus\n---\n\n```ts\ntype VoiceTrainingStatus = \"ready\" | \"training\" | \"failed\";\n```\n\nDefined in: [packages/ai/src/types.ts:2906](https://github.com/TanStack/ai/blob/main/packages/ai/src/types.ts#L2906)\n\nWhether a created voice is usable.\n\n- `'ready'` — usable in `generateSpeech()` now. Every adapter today returns\n  this, because they all finish the voice inside `generateVoice()`.\n- `'training'` — the provider accepted the request but is still building\n  the voice, so it is not usable yet. Reserved for providers that train\n  asynchronously; no adapter returns it yet, and reading the state back\n  will land with the first adapter that needs it.\n- `'failed'` — the provider finished without producing a usable voice.\n"}
